From f193671f9b4e834c39f9c0c1fe58522b86e6b05f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 22:55:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Documentation of the MGIS_REAL_TYPE variable

The installation page and the release notes of version 3.2 describe the
MGIS_REAL_TYPE variable (double or float), the check of the numerical
type of the entry points generated by MFront at loading, and the bindings
requiring double.
---
 docs/web/install.md           |  8 ++++++++
 docs/web/release-notes-3.2.md | 15 +++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/docs/web/install.md b/docs/web/install.md
index b01d281..84b6a27 100644
--- a/docs/web/install.md
+++ b/docs/web/install.md
@@ -120,6 +120,14 @@ generated by the `TFEL` project.
 - `CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE`           : two values are supported `Release` and `Debug`
 - `CASTEM_INSTALL_PATH`        : specify where the castem has been installed
 - `CMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE`       : specify a tool chain file
+- `MGIS_REAL_TYPE`             : numerical type of `MGIS`, `double`
+                                 (default) or `float`. The libraries
+                                 generated by `MFront` must use the same
+                                 type (`real_type` DSL option of
+                                 `mfront`): the type of each entry point
+                                 is checked when it is loaded. The
+                                 `python`, `fortran`, `FEniCS` and `julia`
+                                 bindings require `double`.
 - `Python_ADDITIONAL_VERSIONS` : select the `python` version to
   			         use. Note that only the major and minor
   			         version of python shall be passed, not
diff --git a/docs/web/release-notes-3.2.md b/docs/web/release-notes-3.2.md
index 57bfea4..cf7980a 100644
--- a/docs/web/release-notes-3.2.md
+++ b/docs/web/release-notes-3.2.md
@@ -72,6 +72,21 @@ The following options control the support of the `HDF5` library:
 - `enable-hdf5-automatic-support`: if set, `MGIS` tries by default to
   support `HDF5` even if `enable-hdf5-support` is not set.
 
+### Numerical type
+
+The `MGIS_REAL_TYPE` variable selects the numerical type of `MGIS`:
+`double` (default) or `float`. It is written in the generated header
+`MGIS/RealType.h`, included by `MGIS/Config-c.h`, and exported by the
+installed `cmake` configuration. A `MGIS_REAL_TYPE` macro defined by the
+calling code must agree with it. The behaviours and the material
+properties must be generated by `MFront` with the same type (`real_type`
+DSL option, `TFEL` 5.2): the size of the numerical type of each entry
+point (`<name>_real_size` symbol, `double` if it is not defined) is
+checked when it is loaded, with a message giving both types, and the
+expected versions of the interfaces are shifted by 1000 for another type
+than `double`, as in `MFront`. The `python`, `fortran`, `FEniCS` and
+`julia` bindings require `double`.
+
